    "words": [
      "frighten-v",
      "scare-v",
      "terrify-v"
    ],
    "note": "**Scare** is the everyday word: *the dog scared me*. **Frighten** means the same but sounds a little more serious and is common in writing: *the news frightened many people*. **Terrify** is much stronger: *flying terrifies her* means she is extremely afraid of it."
